CODEFLUX CHANGE LOG

Purpose
-------
This tracked ledger records completed commit-level outcomes. Every authorized
commit must add one focused entry and carry the matching Change-Log trailer.

Commit binding
--------------
An entry uses a stable Change-ID because a commit cannot contain its own final
hash. The commit message must include:

Change-Log: CL-YYYYMMDD-NNN

Resolve the final commit with:

git log --grep="Change-Log: CL-YYYYMMDD-NNN"

Entry fields
------------
Change-ID:
Date:
Type:
Request-or-TODO:
Outcome:
Affected-behavior:
Compatibility-or-migration:
Verification:
Dev-Log:

Entries
-------
Change-ID: CL-20260801-008
Date: 2026-08-01
Type: Execution surfaces, glyph removal, and end-to-end console coverage
Request-or-TODO: The streaming execution surfaces shown in the design mockups,
  and end-to-end browser coverage of the wired console
Outcome: Added web/frontend/executionview -- a measurement strip with
  sparklines, an ordered execution timeline, a severity-filtered streaming log,
  and a currently-executing panel -- projected from durable events and mounted
  in the task workspace. Removed the last decorative glyphs from accessible
  names. Added an end-to-end suite that builds the assets, starts the real
  executable, and drives the console it serves
Affected-behavior: A running task now shows what it is doing: the figures that
  decide whether to intervene, the steps it has taken in the coordinator's own
  order, the lines it is emitting with severity filters, and the unit of work
  in flight. A figure the coordinator has not reported reads as unknown rather
  than as a zero. Decorative glyphs no longer reach assistive technology: a
  section previously announced as "Identity and plan up-arrowhead" and a
  control as "white diamond Request review"
Compatibility-or-migration: No schema change. RootProps, AppShellProps,
  RouteShellProps and TaskWorkspaceProps gain an optional Execution field;
  contextControl no longer takes a glyph
Verification: `go build ./...`, `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build ./web/...`,
  `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l`, `go test ./...`, `codeflux-dev lint`,
  `generate-check`, `migration-check`, and `artifact-check` pass. The new
  end-to-end suite ran against the real executable and passed every check:
  the client mounts with no console error, nothing is fetched from off the
  machine, every heading resolves a colour and a size, the title resolves to
  the reading serif, the navigation rail draws its icons, every primary route
  navigates, keyboard focus is visible, and the page does not scroll sideways
