Change-ID: CL-20260801-007
Date: 2026-08-01
Type: Interface composition, drawn icon set, and live review decisions
Request-or-TODO: AUDIT-024; user direction to make the interface much better
  after visual inspection of the running server
Outcome: Replaced every Unicode glyph used as an icon with a drawn set,
  rebuilt the application bar so its controls fit and stay legible, rebuilt the
  first-run steps as single coherent cards, and connected the four review
  decisions to the coordinator that already implements them
Affected-behavior: The application bar previously truncated its context chips
  to two characters -- "co", "m", "uncom", "provid" -- because a slogan and a
  cost readout shared a track with them; the slogan is gone, the readout moved
  in with the session state, and every chip now shows its full label at one
  height. Navigation, context, and control icons are drawn rather than typed,
  so they render at one weight instead of six. A first-run step is one card
  carrying its position, name, state, meaning, and action, replacing a tall box
  with a heading and a lot of nothing. Accept, request repair, reject, and
  rollback are dispatchable where the review material is loaded; they were
  presented as permanently unavailable against a server that implements all
  four
Compatibility-or-migration: No schema change. primitives.ButtonProps gains an
  Icon field; headerIconButton and its ID variant now take an IconName;
  bindAuthoritativeTimelineActions takes a review decision binder
Verification: `go build ./...`, `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build ./web/...`,
  `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l`, `go test ./...`, `codeflux-dev lint`,
  `generate-check`, `migration-check`, and `artifact-check` pass. The result
  was inspected in a real browser at each step and rebuilt against the running
  server between passes
