Change-ID: CL-20260801-006
Date: 2026-08-01
Type: Frontend asset pipeline, worker launch, and typographic direction
Request-or-TODO: AUDIT-020, AUDIT-021; user request to wire the development
  server and redesign the interface around serif typography and negative space
Outcome: Added `codeflux-dev build-frontend` and `codeflux-dev serve`, taught
  `codeflux start` to resolve browser assets and refuse to run without them,
  gave the frontend server a resolved-asset source so a released executable can
  serve from inside itself, connected a started task to a real worker
  subprocess through a new run launcher, and reset the typographic direction so
  the face a value is set in says what kind of thing it is
Affected-behavior: `codeflux start` now serves the interface. It previously
  started the coordinator, printed a URL, and returned 404 there, because
  nothing ever passed it an asset directory and nothing ever built one.
  Starting a task now creates its Git worktree, queues the run, and launches
  the worker; it previously wrote a run row and returned, so the task read as
  running while no subprocess existed and no provider request was ever made.
  Headings across the frontend now set their own colour and size: the
  first-run title had no colour of its own and rendered near-white on
  near-white in the light theme, and a rail heading had no class at all and
  rendered larger than the page title beside it
Compatibility-or-migration: No schema change. `codeflux start` gains
  `--assets` and honours `CODEFLUX_ASSETS`; with neither, it uses the
  development build directory and otherwise exits 3 naming the build command.
  frontendserver.Options gains an Assets source and refuses both inputs at
  once. coordinator.NewTaskLifecycleAdapter now requires a run launcher
Verification: `go build ./...`, `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build ./web/...`,
  `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l`, `go test ./...`, `codeflux-dev lint`,
  `generate-check`, `migration-check`, and `artifact-check` pass. The built
  executable was started and its URL fetched: index, runtime shim, client, and
  bootstrap all serve. The real client was loaded in headless Chromium and
  mounts with no console or page errors
