Change-ID: CL-20260801-002
Date: 2026-08-01
Type: Test harness, security and abuse suites, benchmarks, and observability
Request-or-TODO: M22-001 through M22-130 and M22-G01 through M22-G06;
  completes Milestone 22
Outcome: Added the deterministic provider, repository, database, event, and
  fault fixtures; the coordinator, browser, and replay harnesses with twelve
  named scenarios; security and abuse suites for the frontend server, Git
  workspace, review editor, executor, storage, redaction, and graph; fuzz
  targets for identity, replay, path resolution, and transport conversion;
  the thirteen-journey browser and accessibility matrix bound to its render
  fixture; twelve declared benchmarks with a recorded environment; the
  metrics, scorecard, and read-only inspection repositories; developer
  diagnostics for logs, profiling, and marks; and an artifact secret scan
  wired into artifact-check
Affected-behavior: Four product defects the new suites found are fixed. The
  HTTP guard now accepts "localhost", which internal/config accepts as a bind
  host and which RFC 6761 reserves for loopback, so a supported configuration
  is no longer locked out of its own interface with a 421. The Git workspace
  and review editor guards now refuse os.ModeIrregular, because Windows
  reports a directory junction that way and filepath.EvalSymlinks returns a
  junction unchanged, so a junction escaped the worktree boundary. Upward
  message pagination no longer replaces every loaded message with a zero
  value. Every routed region now carries an accessible name
Compatibility-or-migration: No schema change. Message bodies are now bounded
  at 64 KiB on append; longer bodies are refused rather than truncated
Verification: `go build ./...`, `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build ./web/...`,
  `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l`, `go test ./...`, `codeflux-dev lint`,
  `generate-check`, `migration-check`, and `artifact-check` pass at this
  commit; the thirteen mounted browser journeys were additionally run for
  real in headless Chromium and pass; the benchmark suite was run and its
  measured figures recorded in docs/benchmarks.md
