Change-ID: CL-20260731-073
Date: 2026-07-31
Type: Deterministic project-memory foundation
Request-or-TODO: M21-001 through M21-028, M21-051 through M21-063, M21-090
  through M21-099, M21-100 through M21-102, M21-108 through M21-125,
  M21-146 through M21-152, M21-157 through M21-163, and M21-169 through
  M21-175
Outcome: Added the governed project-memory domain vocabulary, its immutable
  SQLite schema and repositories, the versioned task fingerprint, atom
  documentation extraction and admission, atom naming identity and rename
  classification, and the project-memory inspection and correction surface.
  Each block was then adversarially reviewed, and every reproduced defect
  found was fixed with a test that failed beforehand.
Affected-behavior: Memory artifacts carry maturity states whose authority
  grants require corroborated evidence bound to the exact revision, so a proof
  earned for one artifact cannot promote another. Quarantine is terminal:
  correction of a terminal artifact is refused rather than silently returning
  it to candidate under its original identity. Deletion previews are computed
  transitively over derived_from, verified against the current lineage index,
  and acknowledged by explicit dependent identity rather than a bare flag.
  Agent self-report is stored but can never satisfy an authority grant.
  Fingerprints hash only exact identity fields, normalized for path separator
  and Unicode form. Atom documentation rejects control bytes that previously
  allowed two different documents to collide on one normalized hash.
Compatibility-or-migration: Adds migration 000025 and its generated catalog
  and version entries. Extends internal/domain with memory types and three ID
  kinds. golang.org/x/text is now a direct dependency. No handwritten
  JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, or CSS source is added. No prior migration
  checksum changed.
Verification: go build, go vet, gofmt, migration-check, and the js/wasm web
  build are clean across the repository. Domain, storage, fingerprint,
  atomdoc, atomname, memoryinspector, and i18n suites pass, including the full
  storage suite against real temporary SQLite databases. Cross-project,
  immutability, quarantine-terminality, and cascade boundaries were exercised
  by raw SQL against a migrated database, and the counterexample boundary was
  confirmed to fail open before its trigger and Go check were added.
Dev-Log: DL-20260731-074

